---
import ComponentDoc from '../../layouts/ComponentDoc.astro';
import Section from '@esa/docs/Section.astro';
import Preview from '@esa/docs/Preview.astro';
import ApiTable from '../../components/ApiTable.astro';
import AlertBox from '@esa/ecology/esa-alert-box.astro';
import { withBase } from '@esa/docs/base';

// Prose only — names, types and defaults are generated from the component
// source by src/data/component-api.ts, so this table cannot drift.
const describe = {
  variant: "Tone — drives the background, border, and auto-mapped icon.",
  title: "Optional bold heading above the message.",
  dismissable: "Shows a close button that hides the alert and emits a dismissed event. Dismissing moves focus to the next focusable element after the box, rather than dropping it to the top of the document.",
  live: "Announce the box when it is injected into an already-loaded page. Off by default, and deliberately so — see Accessibility below. Ignored (with a console warning) when combined with dismissable, because a live region announces a button as bare text and gives no way to reach it.",
};

const events = [
  { name: 'dismissed', type: 'CustomEvent', description: 'Bubbles when the close button is clicked (dismissable only).' },
];
---
<ComponentDoc name="Alert Box" category="Display" slug="esa-alert-box" type=".astro" status="stable"
  summary="Inline status message with a variant-mapped icon, optional title, and optional dismiss control.">

  <Section id="preview" title="Preview">
    <Preview align="start" code={`<AlertBox variant="info" title="Heads up">
  This is an informational message.
</AlertBox>`}>
      <div style="width: 100%;">
        <AlertBox variant="info" title="Heads up">This is an informational message.</AlertBox>
      </div>
    </Preview>
  </Section>

  <Section id="variants" title="Variants">
    <Preview align="start" code={`<AlertBox variant="info" title="Heads up">This is an informational message.</AlertBox>
<AlertBox variant="success" title="Saved">Your changes were saved successfully.</AlertBox>
<AlertBox variant="warning" title="Check this">Some fields need your attention.</AlertBox>
<AlertBox variant="danger" title="Error">Something went wrong while saving.</AlertBox>`}>
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; width: 100%;">
        <AlertBox variant="info" title="Heads up">This is an informational message.</AlertBox>
        <AlertBox variant="success" title="Saved">Your changes were saved successfully.</AlertBox>
        <AlertBox variant="warning" title="Check this">Some fields need your attention.</AlertBox>
        <AlertBox variant="danger" title="Error">Something went wrong while saving.</AlertBox>
      </div>
    </Preview>
  </Section>

  <Section id="states" title="States">
    <p>The title is optional — omit it for a compact single-line alert. With <code>dismissable</code>, a close button appears and a <code>dismissed</code> event bubbles on click.</p>
    <Preview align="start" code={`<AlertBox variant="info">A compact, single-line alert with just a message.</AlertBox>
<AlertBox variant="warning" title="Dismiss me" dismissable={true}>Click the × to hide this alert.</AlertBox>`}>
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; width: 100%;">
        <AlertBox variant="info">A compact, single-line alert with just a message.</AlertBox>
        <AlertBox variant="warning" title="Dismiss me" dismissable={true}>Click the × to hide this alert.</AlertBox>
      </div>
    </Preview>
  </Section>

  <Section id="api" title="API">
    <ApiTable slug="esa-alert-box" describe={describe} events={events} />
  </Section>

  <Section id="accessibility" title="Accessibility">
    <h3>It is not a live region, despite the name</h3>
    <p>
      An alert box is the component most likely to be injected at runtime, so making it
      <code>role="alert"</code> by default looks obvious. It is wrong for the general case,
      for three reasons that compound:
    </p>
    <ul class="a11y">
      <li>It takes a <strong>slot</strong>. Live regions announce raw text with no structure, so a slotted link or button is read as a run-on sentence with no roles. The component cannot see what you put in there.</li>
      <li><code>dismissable</code> puts a <strong>control</strong> inside it. A live region does not take focus and cannot be navigated to, so the user is told a button exists and given no route to it. A message with a control in it is a dialog — use <a href={withBase('/components/esa-dialog')}>esa-dialog</a>.</li>
      <li>Most alert boxes are <strong>present at page load</strong>, where there is no change for a live region to report — or worse, where some screen readers read it out on load as noise.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      So <code>live</code> is opt-in. Turn it on only when all three hold: the box appears in
      response to something the user did, it is not dismissable, and its slot is plain text.
      <code>danger</code> then announces assertively (<code>role="alert"</code>); the other
      variants wait for a pause (<code>role="status"</code>). Combining <code>live</code> with
      <code>dismissable</code> is ignored and warns in the console.
    </p>

    <h3>Everything else</h3>
    <ul class="a11y">
      <li>Icons are auto-mapped per variant (info / circle-check / triangle-alert / circle-alert) and marked <code>aria-hidden</code>.</li>
      <li>The dismiss button has an <code>aria-label="Dismiss"</code>.</li>
      <li>Dismissing moves focus to the next focusable element after the box. Hiding the box removes the button that had focus, and without this focus falls to <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> — silently returning a keyboard user to the top of the document.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

</ComponentDoc>
